# EXERCISE 24 - CREATE AND RESOLVE A MERGE CONFLICT

# ============================================================

# THEORY

#

# A merge conflict occurs when Git cannot automatically decide

# which version of a file should be kept.

# STEP 1

#

# Create a branch:

git switch -c feature/conflict-test

# STEP 2

#

# Modify the same line in main.py.

#

# Example:

#

# print("Version from feature branch")

# Commit:

git add main.py

git commit -m "Update main message"

# STEP 3

#

# Switch to main:

git switch main

# Modify the same line differently.

#

# Example:

#

# print("Version from main branch")

# Commit:

git add main.py

git commit -m "Update main message from main"

# STEP 4

#

# Merge:

git merge feature/conflict-test

# Git may report a conflict.

# STEP 5

#

# Open main.py.

#

# You may see something like:

#

# <<<<<<< HEAD

# Version from main branch

# =======

# Version from feature branch

# >>>>>>> feature/conflict-test

#

#

# Choose the correct version.

#

# Remove:

#

# <<<<<<<

# =======

# >>>>>>>

#

#

# Then:

git add main.py

git commit -m "Resolve merge conflict"

